+## Cancel queued work with an `AbortSignal`
+
+Pass a `signal` to reject queued tasks from anywhere in your app, for example when the user navigates away. Tasks that are already running still settle normally:
+
+```js
+import pLimit from 'p-limit';
+
+const controller = new AbortController();
+const limit = pLimit({concurrency: 5, signal: controller.signal});
+
+const urls = getUrls(); // Assume this returns a large list of URLs
+
+const results = await Promise.allSettled(urls.map(url => limit(async () => {
+	const response = await fetch(url, {signal: controller.signal});
+	return response.json();
+})));
+
+// Elsewhere, for example on route change:
+controller.abort();
+```
+
+Forwarding the same signal to `fetch` also aborts the in-flight requests, which `p-limit` cannot do on its own.
+
